# Nothing here may reach a public repository.
#
# The same three categories `make_release.py` refuses to put in a zip. A
# public repo is worse than a zip for getting this wrong: history is awkward
# to scrub once something is pushed.

# --- VRC's car data ---------------------------------------------------------
# Their paid work. The app unpacks it at runtime from the copy each user
# already owns; no part of it belongs in here. `out/` is a scratch folder that
# still holds an unpacked copy from before that change.
out/
*.acd
**/fa26_unpacked/
**/data_unpacked/

# --- your own driving and setups --------------------------------------------
# Lap telemetry says where and how you drive; .bak files are copies of your
# setups.
*.csv
*.bak
**/fa26_baseline/*.csv
**/maps/

# --- FIA source documents ---------------------------------------------------
# Published by the FIA, not by this project. The findings cite them; the PDFs
# themselves do not need redistributing.
docs/sources/

# --- the FA25 tool ----------------------------------------------------------
# A separate, earlier program for a different car. The two files FA26 needs
# out of it -- carphysics.py and acd.py -- live in core/ instead. These stay
# on disk so that tool keeps working; they are simply not part of this
# repository.
fa25opt/
logger/fa25_baseline/
Run Optimizer.bat
docs/FINDINGS.md

# --- local instrumentation --------------------------------------------------
# A build that records every solve, for improving the model. It changes no
# tracked file -- it wraps the app's methods at start-up -- so the program
# testers run stays byte-identical to the program measured here. It is not
# published, and neither are the records.
dev_run.py
dev_entry.py
dev_floor.py
Run FA26 Optimizer (dev).bat
runs/

# --- build output -----------------------------------------------------------
build/
dist/
*.spec
*.zip
ui/app.ico

# --- working files ----------------------------------------------------------
backup_pre_*/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.log
fa26_error.log
